<article class="env-lemma" id="0CQD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CQD">Lemma <span data-tag="0CQD">15.89.3</span>.</a> Let $K = (K_ n^\bullet )$ be an object of $D(\textit{Mod}(\mathbf{N}, (A_ n)))$. There exists a canonical distinguished triangle </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits K \to \prod \nolimits _ n K_ n^\bullet \to \prod \nolimits _ n K_ n^\bullet \to R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits K[1]  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(A)$. In other words, $R\mathop{\mathrm{lim}}\nolimits K$ is a derived limit of the inverse system $(K_ n^\bullet )$ of $D(A)$, see Derived Categories, Definition <a href="/tag/08TC" data-tag="08TC">13.34.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The proof is exactly the same as the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/07KX" data-tag="07KX">15.88.9</a> using Lemma <a href="/tag/091D" data-tag="091D">15.89.1</a> in stead of Lemma <a href="/tag/07KW" data-tag="07KW">15.88.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>